# Version control and CI
.git
.github

# Claude Code settings
.claude

# Helm charts — not needed by most image builds. Exception: Dockerfile.test
# needs charts/scoreboard (+ its local file://../falco-ctf-common chart
# dependency, P21 item 5) to `helm template`
# charts/scoreboard/templates/ingress-journey.yaml for the ADR-0021 (Issue
# #238, Hard Invariant I15) ingress-participant-route-coverage test.
#
# review-5x R5-F2: an earlier version of this comment claimed "every OTHER
# Dockerfile using this root context ... never COPYs charts/", which is only
# true for scoreboard/auth-policy/collector's Dockerfiles (each COPYs
# explicit narrow paths — go.mod/cmd/<bin>/internal/<pkg>/…, never charts/)
# and Dockerfile.gen (COPYs only docs/ and api/). Dockerfile.tidy does
# `COPY . .` (its whole point is `go mod tidy` seeing every source file that
# might import something), so widening this file DOES put charts/scoreboard
# and charts/falco-ctf-common into ITS build context too. That has no
# functional effect — Dockerfile.tidy's `export` stage only ever copies
# go.mod/go.sum back out (see that Dockerfile's final COPY --from=tidy
# lines), so no chart content reaches `make tidy`'s output — but it DOES
# mean a future edit to charts/scoreboard/** invalidates Docker's build
# cache for `make tidy`'s `COPY . .` layer (and everything after it) even
# though tidy's actual output can't change. Purely a build-cache-locality
# cost, not a correctness one.
#
# `charts/*` (exclude each DIRECT child) + `!charts/<name>/` (re-include
# specific children) is the standard "exclude everything except these"
# idiom — NOT the same as excluding `charts/` itself and trying to
# re-include a file nested inside it, which .dockerignore/.gitignore
# semantics do NOT support (a negation cannot resurrect a path under an
# already fully-excluded parent). Re-including the directory ENTRY itself
# via `charts/*` + `!charts/scoreboard/` is the supported form: once
# re-included, nothing further excludes its own contents.
charts/*
!charts/scoreboard/
!charts/falco-ctf-common/

# Scan output
scan-logs/

# Secrets and local state
*.db
.env
*.pem
*.key
*.cert
